  <h2 id="short-answer">The short answer to "is digital marketing a good career in India"</h2>

  <p>
    Digital marketing is a real, growing field in India, not a dying trend and not a get-rich-quick shortcut either.
    But "is digital marketing good" and "will I personally land a good digital marketing job easily" are two
    different questions, and most course-marketing pages and forum threads blur them together until you cannot tell
    which one is actually being answered.
  </p>

  <p>
    The honest split is this: real channel skill — someone who can run a campaign end to end and show what it
    actually moved — is in short supply and paid well. A resume that says "digital marketing" because of one
    weekend certificate and no shipped campaign is competing against dozens of nearly identical resumes for the
    same junior opening.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      This is not the "anyone can become a digital marketer and work from a beach" pitch that flooded Instagram a
      few years ago, and it is not the "AI killed digital marketing" panic making rounds now either. Both are
      wrong. The field split into two tiers as AI tools matured — a specialist tier that is genuinely short on
      people, and a generalist, certificate-only tier that is genuinely crowded — and most career advice has not
      caught up to that split yet.
    </p>
  </div>

